          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often does guidance describe checking thyroid function once treatment is stable?",
          "answer": "The retrieved guidance does not say how often to check thyroid function once treatment is stable. The passages I found only cover the period after starting treatment or changing the dose.\n\nThe Endocrinology and thyroid association guidance (*Hypothyroidism: which test comes first, and the monitoring interval after a change*) says the thyroid-stimulating hormone test is rechecked six to eight weeks after starting levothyroxine or after any dose change. That is because it takes about that long to settle at the new level. The passage cuts off before any longer interval.\n\nTo find the answer, a clinician or the full version of that document would need to be checked. The question of when routine checks can be spaced out is one to raise with the prescribing clinician.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
